 query the calendar for a UTC range from November 10 to 11 to gather events. I'll also check for any file links related to a spreadsheet the user might have mentioned, and draft a reply accordingly. It looks like I need to read both the message and calendar to align everything.\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Coordinating calendar events**\\n\\nI plan to combine email reading and calendar listing for current information. The email timestamp indicates it's likely November 9, 2026, which may be considered tomorrow from the user's view. I’ll query for events from November 9, 12:00 UTC to November 11, 12:00 UTC to capture local date-dependent events. I'll focus on filtering events within this time range, ensuring I account for time zones so I can accurately present local events for November 10.\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Organizing tasks efficiently**\\n\\nI’m planning to read the email, check the calendar, and access the drive simultaneously. This parallel approach should help me gather all the necessary information more efficiently. By managing these tasks at the same time, I can streamline my workflow and ensure I’m not missing anything important. It’s all about keeping everything in sync so I can provide the best support for the user. Let’s get started!\"}]},\"output_index\":0,\"sequence_number\":277}\n\nevent: response.output_item.added\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.output_item.added\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"ctc_0c2011334cca2e77016af12a1f72d887d0a4577a1c3cea252d\",\"type\":\"custom_tool_call\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"call_id\":\"call_bBwlGiBepxwr1w5QeVYIPKdx\",\"input\":\"\",\"name\":\"codemode\"},\"output_index\":1,\"sequence_number\":278}\n\nevent: response.custom_tool_call_input.delta\ndata: {\"type\":\"response.custom_tool_call_input.delta\",\"delta\":\"const\",\"item_id\":\"ctc_0c2011334cca2e77016af12a1f72d887d0a4577a1c3cea252d\",\"obfuscation\":\"XaKyigTRz2N\",\"output_index\":1,\"sequence_number\":279}\n\nevent: response.custom_tool